# 2️⃣ Maximum Path Sum

## 📖 Problem

Find the maximum sum of values along any path in a Binary Tree.

The path can start and end at any nodes.

Example:

```text
        -10
        /  \
       9    20
           /  \
          15   7
```

Maximum path:

```text
15 → 20 → 7
```

Sum:

```text
42
```

---

## 💡 Important Idea

For every node:

```text
Left Gain
+
Current Node
+
Right Gain
```

This gives the maximum path passing through the current node.

But when returning to the parent, we can only choose **one side**:

```text
Current Node + max(Left Gain, Right Gain)
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
int maxGain(Node* root, int &answer)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return 0;

    int leftGain = max(0, maxGain(root->left, answer));

    int rightGain = max(0, maxGain(root->right, answer));

    int currentPath =
        root->data + leftGain + rightGain;

    answer = max(answer, currentPath);

    return root->data +
           max(leftGain, rightGain);
}

int maxPathSum(Node* root)
{
    int answer = INT_MIN;

    maxGain(root, answer);

    return answer;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(h)
```

