# 4️⃣ Iterative Preorder Traversal

## 📖 Traversal

```text
Root → Left → Right
```

Instead of recursion, use a **Stack**.

---

### Algorithm

```text
Push Root

↓

Pop Node

↓

Process Node

↓

Push Right

↓

Push Left
```

Why push right first?

Because Stack follows:

```text
LIFO
```

So the left child will be processed first.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> preorder(Node* root)
{
    vector<int> result;

    if(root == NULL)
        return result;

    stack<Node*> st;

    st.push(root);

    while(!st.empty())
    {
        Node* current = st.top();
        st.pop();

        result.push_back(current->data);

        if(current->right)
            st.push(current->right);

        if(current->left)
            st.push(current->left);
    }

    return result;
}
```

---

# 5️⃣ Iterative Inorder Traversal

## 📖 Traversal

```text
Left → Root → Right
```

Use a Stack.

---

## 💡 Algorithm

Keep moving left:

```text
Root
 ↓
Left
 ↓
Left
```

Push every node onto the stack.

When there is no left child:

```text
Pop

↓

Process

↓

Move Right
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> inorder(Node* root)
{
    vector<int> result;

    stack<Node*> st;

    Node* current = root;

    while(current != NULL || !st.empty())
    {
        while(current != NULL)
        {
            st.push(current);

            current = current->left;
        }

        current = st.top();
        st.pop();

        result.push_back(current->data);

        current = current->right;
    }

    return result;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(h)
```

---

# 6️⃣ Iterative Postorder Traversal

## 📖 Traversal

```text
Left → Right → Root
```

Postorder is slightly more difficult iteratively.

One common approach uses **two stacks**.

---

### Algorithm

```text
Stack 1

↓

Process Node

↓

Push Left & Right

↓

Stack 2

↓

Reverse Processing
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> postorder(Node* root)
{
    vector<int> result;

    if(root == NULL)
        return result;

    stack<Node*> st1;
    stack<Node*> st2;

    st1.push(root);

    while(!st1.empty())
    {
        Node* current = st1.top();
        st1.pop();

        st2.push(current);

        if(current->left)
            st1.push(current->left);

        if(current->right)
            st1.push(current->right);
    }

    while(!st2.empty())
    {
        result.push_back(st2.top()->data);
        st2.pop();
    }

    return result;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(n)
```

