# 7️⃣ Morris Traversal

## 📖 Definition

Morris Traversal allows us to perform tree traversal with:

```text
O(1)
```

extra space.

It avoids recursion and an explicit stack.

---

## 💡 Morris Inorder Traversal

Traversal:

```text
Left → Root → Right
```

The main idea is to create temporary links between nodes.

---

### Algorithm

For current node:

### Case 1

If there is no left child:

```text
Process current

Move right
```

---

### Case 2

If left child exists:

Find the inorder predecessor.

If predecessor's right is NULL:

```text
Connect predecessor → current

Move left
```

Otherwise:

```text
Remove temporary link

Process current

Move right
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> morrisInorder(Node* root)
{
    vector<int> result;

    Node* current = root;

    while(current != NULL)
    {
        if(current->left == NULL)
        {
            result.push_back(current->data);

            current = current->right;
        }
        else
        {
            Node* predecessor =
                current->left;

            while(predecessor->right != NULL &&
                  predecessor->right != current)
            {
                predecessor =
                    predecessor->right;
            }

            if(predecessor->right == NULL)
            {
                predecessor->right = current;

                current = current->left;
            }
            else
            {
                predecessor->right = NULL;

                result.push_back(current->data);

                current = current->right;
            }
        }
    }

    return result;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Extra Space: O(1)
```

