# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Learn recursive and iterative traversals.

✅ Remember:

```text
Preorder  → Root First

Inorder   → Root Middle

Postorder → Root Last
```

✅ For tree construction, use a Hash Map for efficient inorder lookup.

✅ Use BFS for level-based problems.

✅ Use DFS for path and depth problems.

✅ Learn Morris Traversal for O(1) extra-space traversal.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Mixing preorder and postorder logic.

❌ Forgetting that Postorder's last element is the root.

❌ Not handling NULL nodes.

❌ Forgetting to restore temporary Morris links.

❌ Using O(n²) tree construction by repeatedly searching the inorder array.

❌ Confusing tree height with tree depth.

